// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_regset_8f.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: D-C — reg_set's own refusal of VDP reg $0F, autoincrement (spec §4.2b).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "autoincrement"
//
// $8F04 is a perfectly well-formed register write ($8000..$97FF, not reg $0A), so
// nothing else in the module has an opinion about it. What it does is change the
// VDP's address stride mid-frame, and EVERY span computation in raster_dsl assumes
// stride 2: op_cram_span, op_mask, the ship destination. A band composed against a
// span the hardware then writes at stride 4 is checked against arithmetic that no
// longer describes what happens.
//
// IT DOES NOT CALL raster_program, deliberately. The program-level scan (E-D, its
// own poison next door) would ALSO catch this word, and a poison that trips two
// layers cannot tell you which one is still alive. raster_words walks the same fire
// list without running the scan, so the only thing that can fail here is the
// constructor's own ensure.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_four_bands.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_regset_8f

const POISON_REGSET_8F = [
    fire(100, [reg_set($8F04)]),
]

ensure(raster_words(POISON_REGSET_8F) > 0,
       "poison_regset_8f: raster_words returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the constructor it targets")
